<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Martim Afonso de Sousa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1500–<a href="/years/1571">1571</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Martim Afonso de Sousa was a Portuguese nobleman and naval commander who led the first official colonising expedition to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> in 1530 to 1533. In 1532 he founded São Vicente, the first permanent Portuguese town in Brazil, and was granted the captaincy of São Vicente. He later served as governor of Portuguese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> from 1542 to 1545.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/martim-afonso-de-sousa.jpg" alt="Martim Afonso de Sousa" width="320" height="615" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Martim_Afonso_de_Sousa_(Archaeological_Survey_of_India,_Goa).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
